  "decision_reason": "Forced inlining removes the helper symbol and expands Point2 equality from 340 to 443 machine-code bytes. Exact witnesses match and rational query medians improve by 56\u201383%. Other timings remain variable, including a 17.3% higher pi-transport repeat median and broad construction/preparation variation. The query aggregate alone (251.213 versus 235.143 ms) does not support retaining this change over the unresolved symbolic costs. All measured Point2 shortcut variants remain unadmitted.",
  "next_step": "Restore the original Point2 equality implementation. Independently validate and retain only the exact affine, near-coincident, unknown, abort and concurrent equality regressions plus the conservative-equality documentation on isolated admitted production source. Do not run or claim optimization admission or application speedups.",
  "limitations": "Five fresh processes per version and mode, CPU 0, alternating order. No counting allocator in timing binaries; memory counts requested Rust bytes and excludes allocator metadata/native heaps. Eight point families, including shared-handle and copied-coordinate controls. First is a new pair, not empty global caches. Construction and explicit numerical preparation are measured separately. This scalar/point early gate does not admit full application behavior or production source.",
